====================================================================================================
v134  FEATURE WIDTH vs THE BARREN-PLATEAU REGIME
====================================================================================================
  v99 measured width 0.96 / 0.99 of the path at efficient_su2(reps=1),
  N=4/6 - a shallow low-M ansatz with NO plateau. This asks whether width
  falls as the plateau regime is entered, which is where the walk's
  precondition would actually be met.

  The SENSING oracle's job is cost and v89 proves it cannot help a
  plateau. Landscape navigation is the WALK's job. TIER B - exact
  Statevector energies, no shots, no walk run.

  TWO COST FUNCTIONS, because the choice decides whether a plateau exists
  at all. A LOCAL cost (Heisenberg, 2-local) plateaus only at depth
  ~poly(N); a GLOBAL cost |<0..0|psi>|^2 plateaus at shallow depth. A first
  run used the local cost alone, and its variance fell only 5x from N=4 to
  N=10 - it never entered the regime, so it could say nothing about it.

  LOCAL  (Heisenberg)
      N   reps    M    Var(dE/dtheta_0)    feature width (frac of path)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      4     1    16      4.029e-01          0.1532 +- 0.0290
      4     4    40      3.606e-01          0.0975 +- 0.0174

      6     1    24      4.700e-01          0.1343 +- 0.0290
      6     4    60      1.905e-01          0.1017 +- 0.0176

      8     1    32      4.430e-01          0.1460 +- 0.0296
      8     4    80      1.376e-01          0.1061 +- 0.0260

     10     1    40      3.696e-01          0.1468 +- 0.0334
     10     4   100      8.868e-02          0.0934 +- 0.0198

  GLOBAL |<0..0|psi>|^2
      N   reps    M    Var(dE/dtheta_0)    feature width (frac of path)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      4     1    16      4.176e-03          0.1580 +- 0.0330
      4     4    40      2.260e-03          0.1043 +- 0.0375

      6     1    24      6.298e-04          0.1476 +- 0.0301
